(6604478, 984923, 101702, '<td valign="top">The standout image of the challenge by a long way.</td>', 'The standout image of the challenge by a long way.', '2011-11-27 17:08:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(6604521, 984344, 108069, '<td valign="top">Outstanding. Not only is this a beautiful photo, it''s a clinic in when and how to use HDR. Crisp and clear, no halos whatsoever mixed in the white bark vs. blue sky, excellent detail and depth throughout, masterfully exposed. Excellent photo and absolutely perfect for this challenge.</td>', 'Outstanding. Not only is this a beautiful photo, it''s a clinic in when and how to use HDR. Crisp and clear, no halos whatsoever mixed in the white bark vs. blue sky, excellent detail and depth throughout, masterfully exposed. Excellent photo and absolutely perfect for this challenge.', '2011-11-27 18:01:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(6604524, 984773, 108069, '<td valign="top">Beautiful photo. Nice ratio of sky to earth. Nicely exposed throughout, as it should be with HDR. Well done.</td>', 'Beautiful photo. Nice ratio of sky to earth. Nicely exposed throughout, as it should be with HDR. Well done.', '2011-11-27 18:03:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(6604525, 984685, 108069, '<td valign="top">Lovely photo. Rich and crisp. Very nice.</td>', 'Lovely photo. Rich and crisp. Very nice.', '2011-11-27 18:04:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(6604529, 984769, 108069, '<td valign="top">Love the sun flares and grain. Lovely photo.</td>', 'Love the sun flares and grain. Lovely photo.', '2011-11-27 18:11:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(6604532, 984825, 108069, '<td valign="top">I''m trying to be as annoying as possible and guess who this is: <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=86218" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">RianBotes</a> is the only DPCer I know that regularly churns out stunning lightning shots such as this. Of course if this is not Rian, please take it as a compliment.<br/> <br/>The sky is just magnificent, and the entire image is as crisp as can be. Awesome photo.</td>', 'I''m trying to be as annoying as possible and guess who this is:  RianBotes is the only DPCer I know that regularly churns out stunning lightning shots such as this. Of course if this is not Rian, please take it as a compliment. The sky is just magnificent, and the entire image is as crisp as can be. Awesome photo.', '2011-11-27 18:15:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(6604535, 984685, 6519, '<td valign="top">Interesting..... this turned out my only 10 in this challenge and I''m not even a real "horsey" person.<br/>I love the HDR effect here - it is so wonderfully subtle, that I''ll have to take your word for it. Lovely subject, tones, composition and focus.</td>', 'Interesting..... this turned out my only 10 in this challenge and I''m not even a real "horsey" person.I love the HDR effect here - it is so wonderfully subtle, that I''ll have to take your word for it. Lovely subject, tones, composition and focus.', '2011-11-27 18:18:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(6604538, 984905, 108069, '<td valign="top">I think I remember this mill! I cannot remember the DPCer or the challenge, but I know this, gosh darn it. This is really well done. Exposure range is great, and the colors are super rich but not so bright, so they add to the gloomy mood created by the mist and the ramshackle mill. Nice one.</td>', 'I think I remember this mill! I cannot remember the DPCer or the challenge, but I know this, gosh darn it. This is really well done. Exposure range is great, and the colors are super rich but not so bright, so they add to the gloomy mood created by the mist and the ramshackle mill. Nice one.', '2011-11-27 18:24:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(6604539, 984799, 108069, '<td valign="top">Beautifully done. Crisp detail, very nice tones, just super pleasing. Lovely photo.</td>', 'Beautifully done. Crisp detail, very nice tones, just super pleasing. Lovely photo.', '2011-11-27 18:25:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6604540, 984701, 108069, '<td valign="top">Texture and then some. Quite busy but also quite interesting. Cool image.</td>', 'Texture and then some. Quite busy but also quite interesting. Cool image.', '2011-11-27 18:25:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(6604543, 984642, 108069, '<td valign="top">Excellent. So incredibly crisp and clean. Very interesting use of exposure management. Front-pager.</td>', 'Excellent. So incredibly crisp and clean. Very interesting use of exposure management. Front-pager.', '2011-11-27 18:28:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(6604546, 984829, 108069, '<td valign="top">Nice scene and well done on the processing.<br/> <br/>In my mind, however, the interesting story here is all that steam blowing into the sky. I''d wager you''ve got a number of shots of this, and I think a slight adjustment in composition/cropping would make this more interesting. I do love what HDR can do with clouds/smoke/steam, so this is really well spotted.</td>', 'Nice scene and well done on the processing. In my mind, however, the interesting story here is all that steam blowing into the sky. I''d wager you''ve got a number of shots of this, and I think a slight adjustment in composition/cropping would make this more interesting. I do love what HDR can do with clouds/smoke/steam, so this is really well spotted.', '2011-11-27 18:31:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(6604547, 984774, 108069, '<td valign="top">Super rich colors and tones give this a great gloom. Storybook sky.<br/> <br/>What I''m about to say is something I cannot do, but with some of the software out there I know it''s possible and I think it might even give this already great image a boost. You obviously know what you''re doing with PP, but consider this... The eye is caught in the front of the photo with the fruits, and then it has to jump over a bit of dulled space to get to the great sky/horizon. But there are more fruits at 9 o''clock and then another closer to the cityscape. The cacti also seem to present a trough right there. With some targeted exposure manipulation of brightening that fruit up a bit and "lighting a path" through the trough, you''d be able to lead the eye from the rich fruit up front, through the cacti to the other fruit, and on to the horizon and sky. Just a theory, of course, but maybe worth playing around with. or it may completely ruin the image.<br/> <br/>Regardless, this is super.</td>', 'Super rich colors and tones give this a great gloom. Storybook sky. What I''m about to say is something I cannot do, but with some of the software out there I know it''s possible and I think it might even give this already great image a boost. You obviously know what you''re doing with PP, but consider this... The eye is caught in the front of the photo with the fruits, and then it has to jump over a bit of dulled space to get to the great sky/horizon. But there are more fruits at 9 o''clock and then another closer to the cityscape. The cacti also seem to present a trough right there. With some targeted exposure manipulation of brightening that fruit up a bit and "lighting a path" through the trough, you''d be able to lead the eye from the rich fruit up front, through the cacti to the other fruit, and on to the horizon and sky. Just a theory, of course, but maybe worth playing around with. or it may completely ruin the image. Regardless, this is super.', '2011-11-27 18:42:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(6604550, 984702, 108069, '<td valign="top">Lovely photo. Beautiful scene presented very nicely.</td>', 'Lovely photo. Beautiful scene presented very nicely.', '2011-11-27 18:44:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(6604551, 984657, 108069, '<td valign="top">Great shot. Beautiful tones and colors, and a wonderful scene with the gulls (great movement included), the pier, summer sunset colors and... Christmas trees?! This may be a very normal scene for you, but there''s a nice unexpected twist to it for me. There''s also something very organic about those pier stanchions, quite possibly because they''re not just silhouettes. This should do quite well.</td>', 'Great shot. Beautiful tones and colors, and a wonderful scene with the gulls (great movement included), the pier, summer sunset colors and... Christmas trees?! This may be a very normal scene for you, but there''s a nice unexpected twist to it for me. There''s also something very organic about those pier stanchions, quite possibly because they''re not just silhouettes. This should do quite well.', '2011-11-27 18:44:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(6604552, 984673, 108069, '<td valign="top">Wow, beautiful scene. I love the contrast between the austere foreground and the richly colored vineyard. I want to congratulate you for catching it at such a wonderful moment to get the light on those vines despite the weather, and then I remembered the challenge and want to congragulate you again on bubling up the very best in this scene for the viewer, regardless of the circumstances. Well done.</td>', 'Wow, beautiful scene. I love the contrast between the austere foreground and the richly colored vineyard. I want to congratulate you for catching it at such a wonderful moment to get the light on those vines despite the weather, and then I remembered the challenge and want to congragulate you again on bubling up the very best in this scene for the viewer, regardless of the circumstances. Well done.', '2011-11-27 18:46:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(6604553, 984743, 108069, '<td valign="top">Fresh and exhilarating scene. Beautiful. The stop-motion waves add to the immediacy and freshness of the image (both as a moment in time and that it''s not another blured out seascape ;) Nice tones, and nice movement in the clouds. I can feel the strong breeze from here.</td>', 'Fresh and exhilarating scene. Beautiful. The stop-motion waves add to the immediacy and freshness of the image (both as a moment in time and that it''s not another blured out seascape ;) Nice tones, and nice movement in the clouds. I can feel the strong breeze from here.', '2011-11-27 18:46:19.000000', NULL, 1);
