(6606575, 984825, 78757, '<td valign="top">That is absolutely beautiful!<br/> <br/>The Voortrekker Monument is one of my most strongly remembered iconographic symbols of South Africa.<br/> <br/>Ek hoe van Suid Afrika! Ek wil terug kom om die pragtige laand weer te seen.<br/> <br/>Baia dankie vir die geheue.</td>', 'That is absolutely beautiful! The Voortrekker Monument is one of my most strongly remembered iconographic symbols of South Africa. Ek hoe van Suid Afrika! Ek wil terug kom om die pragtige laand weer te seen. Baia dankie vir die geheue.', '2011-11-30 14:39:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(6606589, 984868, 116730, '<td valign="top">I would love if you could set up a tutorial on how you did this. I just think this photo is fantastic and would love to learn how to do some really nice HDR</td>', 'I would love if you could set up a tutorial on how you did this. I just think this photo is fantastic and would love to learn how to do some really nice HDR', '2011-11-30 14:59:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(6606595, 984868, 114969, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jesusfreak864ever:</b></div><hr/><i> I would love if you could set up a tutorial on how you did this. I just think this photo is fantastic and would love to learn how to do some really nice HDR </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks, glad you liked it!<br/>The main editing steps are described under the photo. I''m afraid more details would not be very useful (like values and parameters for each step), because they are very specific to the photo and to what you want to achieve. The main HDR itself was done in a very classical way: 3 RAWs, HDR Efex Pro, some quick adjustments and that''s it. Done in 3 minutes (really!). However, tone-mapping the HDR was merely the beginning, and the result is all about many local tweaks (more saturation here, more light there, more detail in the darks here, change the color of that, etc.). This is what took the longest by a large margin (editing-wise). Feel free to PM me if you want specific information.</td>', 'Originally posted by jesusfreak864ever: I would love if you could set up a tutorial on how you did this. I just think this photo is fantastic and would love to learn how to do some really nice HDR   Thanks, glad you liked it!The main editing steps are described under the photo. I''m afraid more details would not be very useful (like values and parameters for each step), because they are very specific to the photo and to what you want to achieve. The main HDR itself was done in a very classical way: 3 RAWs, HDR Efex Pro, some quick adjustments and that''s it. Done in 3 minutes (really!). However, tone-mapping the HDR was merely the beginning, and the result is all about many local tweaks (more saturation here, more light there, more detail in the darks here, change the color of that, etc.). This is what took the longest by a large margin (editing-wise). Feel free to PM me if you want specific information.', '2011-11-30 15:09:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(6606631, 984960, 80096, '<td valign="top">Hey Jamie - I really liked this, gave it a 6. It''s adorable and the quality is excellent. I''m beginning to think we''ve both outgrown DPChallenge. HUGS, Jo ;-)</td>', 'Hey Jamie - I really liked this, gave it a 6. It''s adorable and the quality is excellent. I''m beginning to think we''ve both outgrown DPChallenge. HUGS, Jo ;-)', '2011-11-30 16:36:03.000000', NULL, 0),
